WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.590
- Chelsea, pleasure.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.210
- So good to see you.
- Oh my gosh,

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.530
welcome back.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.460
- This is great.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.750
- I think you're just gonna be a regular.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:07.590
Every time I'm in New York,

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.900
I'm just gonna beg you to
be in my show. (laughs)

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.190
- And I will gladly do it.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.360
- We love you and thank you

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.193
for bringing Maven.

00:00:13.193 --> 00:00:14.610
Maven, thank you for coming back.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.443
- You're welcome.

00:00:15.443 --> 00:00:16.830
- [Kelly] You look beautiful.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.750
- I personally can't believe this.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.640
I'm sitting next to the
secretary's daughter?

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.473
- [Kelly] Have y'all ever met?

00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:23.555
- I've gotta go back and get my GED now.

00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:24.525
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:25.358
I've got to!

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.618
- [Kelly] This is what-
- [Tracy] How'd this happen?

00:00:26.618 --> 00:00:27.900
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.130
- So wait, last time you were here,

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.900
though you mentioned wanting Maven

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.550
to meet strong and powerful women.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.734
So, well, here you go.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.510
(all laugh)

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.880
So what are some questions you get

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.200
from younger women?

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.030
- Well, you know, one
of the things, Maven,

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.340
I'd love to ask you

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.020
because I get asked this a lot,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.960
is when you were little, what did you-

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:49.793
- Even younger.

00:00:49.793 --> 00:00:52.260
- Or even younger,
'cause you're growing up

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.330
as your dad knows, too fast, right?

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.520
What did you wanna be?

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.220
People asked me that all the time.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.560
So if I ask you now, what do you wanna be?

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.210
- A Marine biologist.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.465
- [Hillary] You wanna be a--

00:01:04.465 --> 00:01:06.390
- (gasps) Gosh. That's what
my daughter wants to be.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.590
- That's so cool.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.600
And when you become a biologist,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.390
what do you wanna study and learn about?

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.443
- Uh, the ocean?

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.010
- And is there a particular animal

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.930
that you really love in the ocean?

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.107
- Shark?
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:20.107 --> 00:01:21.960
That's my daughter's favorite animal.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.220
- [Kelly] Who doesn't?

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.254
- Oh my gosh, she--

00:01:24.254 --> 00:01:25.770
- She has a 20,000 gallon shark tank

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.203
in our backyard.

00:01:27.203 --> 00:01:28.270
- Oh my gosh.
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.060
- 14 or 15 sharks in there.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.890
- [Chelsea] Seriously?
- Black tips, white tips or-

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:32.723
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:01:32.723 --> 00:01:34.890
- Charlotte, turn off the television now.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.690
- Charlotte.
(all laughing)

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.030
- Because we live in an apartment here

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:44.030
in New York City and we
do not have space for...

00:01:44.538 --> 00:01:45.441
- She wanted it.

00:01:45.441 --> 00:01:46.274
She wanted to study--
- [Kelly] That's incredible.

00:01:46.274 --> 00:01:48.720
- So I put like eight tanks in the house.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.640
Have the shark tank outside the house.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.860
She has cone snail from Australia.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.120
- [Hillary] Oh boy.
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.500
- Seven seas in the world.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.570
And the cone snail is
the most dangerous thing

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.500
on the planet.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.370
One cone snail

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.750
can kill a blue whale.
- [Kelly] So why not have 'em

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.583
in your house?

00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:02.880
Cool.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.140
- I'm so glad you've already

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.213
turned the television off.
- [Kelly] Who feeds them?

00:02:06.213 --> 00:02:09.200
- No, No, um, I have a
team of people that come

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.980
and take care of her tanks every day.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.000
- That's so cool.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.170
Oh my God, you must love aquariums.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.450
My kids love aquariums.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.803
- Well, she's got her own in the backyard.

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.080
(all laugh)

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.760
- So some of us don't have huge aquariums

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.593
at our house.

00:02:21.593 --> 00:02:23.010
We have to go to them.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.260
I wanna ask you something though

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.610
because I heard that you have

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.720
like a favorite thing,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.850
your definition of bravery, right?

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.050
What's your definition?

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.930
What do you think that is, to be brave?

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.300
- Mm something you do dangerous,

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.250
but you do it anyways.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.995
- [Kelly] All right. I love that.

00:02:39.995 --> 00:02:41.220
(audience clapping)

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.900
You know what, you only get one life.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.340
Try. Yeah.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:45.270
- You have to be brave.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.490
She understands that, she knows that.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:48.870
You have to do the things that-

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.170
it takes a lot of guts
to go for your dreams.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.910
So I want her to know that you have to-

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.530
because one thing that stops us

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.423
in our lives is the word, if.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.850
What if it doesn't work?
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.560
- No, you have to keep going.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.670
- [Kelly] What if it does?
- If it doesn't work,

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.020
you do something else.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:04.860
- Right.
- Yep.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.840
- Were you always brave, like growing up?

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:07.890
Were you always--

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.690
- Well, I think we tried to be.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.440
I mean, I think part of raising children,

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.560
is to give them both
roots and wings. Right?

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.540
You want them to have those standards.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.400
You want them to have those values

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.000
but you also want them
to be able to take risks,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.700
but you know, ones that are reasonable.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.070
And so how do you inculcate that?

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.330
How do you talk about that?

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.580
And I think, talking about

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.490
how you encourage your
nine year old daughter

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.020
to frankly hang out with sharks,

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.370
which, you know,

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.740
I find pretty brave.
- Four eels.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.170
- Um, yeah, no, I think you learn it.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:46.530
And I think it comes from
primarily your family.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:47.790
Sometimes people on the outside,

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.700
a teacher, a coach, a minister,

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.080
somebody else can help you

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.420
but it really does come from your family.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.253
Yeah.

00:03:55.253 --> 00:03:56.190
- I love that you just pointed out

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.023
something though as well.

00:03:57.023 --> 00:03:59.850
Like not all of us, you know, are blessed

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.200
with great fathers.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.070
Like not all of us are.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.440
So what you just said like a village

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.273
can raise a kid.

00:04:05.273 --> 00:04:07.293
Like I didn't have that experience.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.180
But I didn't have that experience.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.100
A lot of people don't
but what is important is

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.980
I had my pastor, Dr. Frankie Rainey.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.620
He would cut out clippings
and send them to me

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.500
of like, "Great job on
this solo thing you did."

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:20.333
And, "Great job."

00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:22.080
And I think that's important.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.550
Like, even if you're not a parent,

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.710
you can still be a father figure

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.330
or a parental figure in some sense.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.335
I love that you said that.
- A positive light,

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.168
a positive force.

00:04:30.168 --> 00:04:31.740
- [Tracy] I had someone there for me.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.170
- So, Tracy, you are on a comedy tour now.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.347
So how'd you come up with the name,

00:04:35.347 --> 00:04:36.750
"No Disrespect?"

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.010
- I'm gonna be saying things

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.796
I don't want anybody
taking in the wrong way.

00:04:39.796 --> 00:04:41.405
(all laughing)

00:04:41.405 --> 00:04:43.208
- It's a warning.

00:04:43.208 --> 00:04:44.670
- Lemme tell you how I feel.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.063
I'm a grown man.

00:04:46.063 --> 00:04:47.220
I'm gonna speak on things.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.330
- Bring football pads.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.749
Too macho.

00:04:49.749 --> 00:04:51.180
- Yeah. Don't take it in the wrong way.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.420
So no disrespect before
we even get started.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.620
No disrespect.
- But Tracy,

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.258
can I ask you because I've been following,

00:04:58.258 --> 00:05:00.570
some comics are getting criticized

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.010
for saying something-
- [Kelly] A lot.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.300
- Offends people and all of that.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.460
- You want a war on free speech,

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.900
an attack on free speech.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.363
- Yeah. But how do you think about that?

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:15.170
Cause I think people who
are in the public eye

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:18.120
should have the same right to free speech

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.380
as anybody else.
- [Tracy] Right.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.340
To me, you got be funny.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.650
- But you gotta be funny about it. Yeah.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.480
- Cause anybody could do comedy.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.460
Anybody could learn how to tell jokes,

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.290
but are you funny?

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.460
- Oh, see, that's like singers.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.786
See, a lot of people can sing,

00:05:30.786 --> 00:05:32.717
but they don't move you.
- But everybody can't sang.

00:05:32.717 --> 00:05:34.930
(all laugh)

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:35.832
Lot of people can sing,

00:05:35.832 --> 00:05:37.692
but everybody can't sang.

00:05:37.692 --> 00:05:39.822
Aretha Franklin can sang.

00:05:39.822 --> 00:05:40.800
- She was pretty good.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.170
- Kelly, I was the kid
at their church choir.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.003
They were always like, "You know,

00:05:44.003 --> 00:05:45.060
we really appreciate Chelsea.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.738
She's always on time."

00:05:46.738 --> 00:05:49.110
(all laugh)

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:50.190
- Punctuality.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.123
- Punctuality.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.150
Also, maybe she should be

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.460
on the bells next year.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.800
- She should pick up an instrument.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:02.790
- I, I think there's like
an attack on free speech.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:06.180
I mean, the stage is sacred.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.920
I should be able to say what I wanna say

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.390
up here on stage.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.410
I'm doing standup.

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:12.361
You know what you paid to come see.

00:06:12.361 --> 00:06:13.194
- Right.

00:06:13.194 --> 00:06:15.690
- You knew that before
you came in the building.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:16.530
Why are you gonna attack me?

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.573
So when Will Smith smacked Chris,

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:20.490
I was hurt.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:22.980
Not just to see a black
man smack another black man

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.467
on the biggest stage in the world.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:25.300
- [Hillary] Right. Right.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.237
- But that he opened the
door for people to think,

00:06:28.237 --> 00:06:31.380
"Oh, if I say something about your wife,

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:33.750
you could come up here and assault me."

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.400
You can't do that.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.780
You couldn't do that to Richard Pryor

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.855
or George Carlin.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:39.855 --> 00:06:41.371
(audience clapping)

00:06:41.371 --> 00:06:42.454
- It's just jokes.

00:06:42.454 --> 00:06:44.070
- Yeah. You know, Chelsea

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.380
and I did a series about gutsy women.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.213
It's called "Gutsy".

00:06:47.213 --> 00:06:49.230
It's gonna premiere in September

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.160
on "Apple TV Plus".

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.690
And we interviewed women comics

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.010
and we did that in part

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:59.070
because some people still
say women can't be funny.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.200
And frankly, I disagree.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.400
- Marsha Warfield?

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.480
- Are you kidding?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.670
And we interviewed Wanda Sykes,

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:06.630
who was telling us,

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.090
who I adore, we interviewed her

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.400
and she was telling us
about how she'd gone

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:16.110
to a big comedy event
that was to raise money

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:17.190
for cancer.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.600
So, I mean, it was a charitable event

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.910
but she and a bunch of
comics were doing it.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.470
And she was the only woman.

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.960
And they were in Boston, I think.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.900
And she had some jokes about politicians

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.070
who shall remain nameless.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.920
And so she had these jokes,

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.150
half the audience laughed

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.563
and half the audience booed.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.310
But the other men who'd been on the stage

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.560
had also had political jokes.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.580
- Yeah.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:42.600
- And people either
laughed or they didn't,

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.530
but they didn't boo.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:44.707
And Wanda was saying like,

00:07:44.707 --> 00:07:46.350
"You know, here I am, right.

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:47.183
I'm out there.

00:07:47.183 --> 00:07:48.300
I'm telling these jokes.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.680
And I'm a woman telling these jokes.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.350
And somehow that produces the boos."

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:54.300
I thought that was really interesting.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:55.890
- And for your daughter, that's my thing.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.443
Like for my daughter, for your kids,

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.320
I want a better world.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.600
I don't want women to
have to keep dancing.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.433
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:04.433 --> 00:08:05.757
Like, I don't wanna dance around it.

00:08:05.757 --> 00:08:07.920
You should be able to
be bold and courageous

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.420
and funny and--
- The female soccer team.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.260
- [Chelsea] Yes they're much better

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.211
than our men.
- I said,

00:08:11.211 --> 00:08:12.044
then give them their money.

00:08:12.044 --> 00:08:13.723
- Yes. Give them their money.

00:08:13.723 --> 00:08:15.210
(audience cheering)

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.350
- [Tracy] Give them their money!

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.150
- All right, we have
to take another break.

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:20.940
Tickets for Tracy's "No
Disrespect" tour on sale right now,

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.413
Y'all go online to get yours.

